cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the manuscript using the metadata below. Cite the published
  distance-spectrum calculation of Howlader and Panigrahi wherever that prior
  result is used.
title: "wow284: Reproducible artifacts for Counterexamples, Spectral Obstructions, and Deletion Stability for WOW-284"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Petkov
    given-names: Samuil
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, École normale supérieure, Université PSL"
    email: samuil.petkov@phys.ens.psl.eu
version: 2.2.4
date-released: 2026-07-28
url: "https://github.com/SamPetkov/wow284"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SamPetkov/wow284"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  WOW-284 asserts a bound relating minimum dual degree and the least distance
  eigenvalue for connected graphs of girth at least five. This release gives
  exact counterexamples of orders 38, 39, 40, 42, and 50 and develops regular
  spectral criteria, degree and diameter obstructions, the exact all-degree
  one-variable nonbacktracking linear-programming optimum, Moore-graph
  puncture spectra, and deletion-stability results. Lean 4.31 kernel-checks
  the complete graph-level 50-vertex proof, finite spectral certificates for
  orders 38, 39, 40, and 42, and the separate analytic LP optimum,
  attainment, and coefficient-level optimizer rigidity.
keywords:
  - distance spectrum
  - dual degree
  - Moore graph
